state/
# ⚠️ `**` MANDATORY — LEAK HOLE found on 06/08/2026 on a PUBLIC repo.
#    `docs/mcp/*.md` only covered level 1 (server). Levels 2 and 3 —
#    `docs/mcp/{server}/{tool}.md`, `{subTool}.md` — were NOT ignored,
#    yet those are the most SPECIFIC docs, hence the most likely to name a
#    client, an amount, an identifier. The hole had been dormant since the
#    3-level granularity was created: nobody had written a level-2 doc yet.
#    A dormant error class is not an absent one. Sealed by
#    `gitignore-gate.test.js` (the rule is tested on FICTITIOUS paths, so it
#    holds on a pristine clone) — reddening proven by real sabotage.
docs/mcp/**/*.md
!docs/mcp/**/*.md.example
docs/session/*.md
!docs/session/*.md.example
# ⚠️ NAMED EXCEPTION (14/08/2026): `language.md` describes THE LANGUAGE itself,
#    not a maintainer's context — zero personal data, useful to ANYONE who
#    clones. It is the single source of the engine's semantics (the doc fleet
#    keeps only a pointer to it): leaving it out of the repo means losing it
#    on a machine change and depriving a pristine clone of the only doc that
#    says what the language does. ⚠️ NEVER widen this exception to another
#    `docs/session/*.md` without checking for personal data — that is the
#    rule this block protects.
!docs/session/language.md
node_modules/
.stryker-tmp/
reports/

# USER config (skill/project names = personal data) — create it from the .example
ctxroute-config.json

# Private DEPLOYMENT terms (never published) — cf leak-gate.test.js
.fuite-perso-local.json

# Internal work journals (maintainer-only, never published)
SWAP-PLAN.md
REFACTOR-PLAN.md
REFACTOR-ARCHIVE.md
EVAL-SESSIONS.md

# ⚠️ TLA+ TOOLING AND GENERATED MODEL CONFIGS (20/08/2026).
#    `tla2tools.jar` is a 2.2 MB BINARY downloaded on demand by
#    `specs/tla/run-tlc.mjs` (release pinned + SHA-256 verified): committing a
#    third-party binary is both dead weight in the history and a supply-chain
#    artifact nobody re-checks. `specs/tla/*.cfg` are GENERATED from
#    `specs/tla/runs.json`, the single source of the run matrix — committing
#    them would create a second truth that drifts, which is exactly what the
#    generation exists to prevent.
specs/tla/tla2tools.jar
specs/tla/*.cfg
